---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Tea & Toast | Our Story & Culinary Philosophy"
  description="Learn about the origin of Tea & Toast, our passion for artisanal breads, homemade spreads, and the slow ritual of brewing loose-leaf tea."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16 space-y-10">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-center space-y-3">
      <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-amber-800 bg-amber-100/80 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">
        Behind the Crust & Cup
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900">
        Our Story: Savoring Life One Slice at a Time
      </h1>
      <p class="text-stone-600 text-base sm:text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        What started in 2020 as a personal passion project celebrating comfort food has grown into a mindful kitchen community.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Image -->
    <div class="rounded-3xl overflow-hidden aspect-[16/9] shadow-md border border-stone-200">
      <img
        src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517433670267-08bbd4be890f?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop"
        alt="Fresh bread and warm teapot on a wooden table"
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <!-- Body Story (E-E-A-T signals for Google Search & AdSense) -->
    <div class="prose prose-stone max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif leading-relaxed text-stone-700 space-y-6">
      <h2>Why "Tea & Toast"?</h2>
      <p>
        In an era of rushed mornings, grab-and-go energy bars, and distracted eating, breakfast has often been reduced to a chore. We believe the exact opposite: <strong>the first 30 minutes of your day set the tone for your entire life.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        There is something intrinsically grounding about the rhythmic sound of slicing into a naturally leavened sourdough loaf, waiting for the toaster chime, hearing the kettle whistle, and watching loose tea leaves slowly unfurl in hot water. 
      </p>

      <h2>Our Culinary Philosophy</h2>
      <p>
        Every single recipe shared on <strong>Tea & Toast</strong> follows four cardinal principles:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Flavor Balance & Contrast:</strong> We pair crunch with creaminess (crisp toast with whipped ricotta or avocado) and warmth with bright acidity (rich butter balanced with citrus bergamot tea).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No-Fuss, Everyday Luxury:</strong> Gourmet does not mean tedious. Most of our toast and spread recipes take fewer than 10 minutes to assemble using accessible, high-quality ingredients.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Mindful Tea Pairing:</strong> Just as fine dining elevates wine pairing, tea possesses intricate flavor profiles—malty, floral, grassy, smoky, and sweet. We test and recommend the exact tea that elevates each dish.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Thoroughly Tested Steps:</strong> We document exact times, temperatures, and troubleshooting tips so you never end up with soggy bread or over-steeped, bitter tea.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Connect With Us</h2>
      <p>
        We love seeing your breakfast setups and afternoon tea moments. Connect with us on social media:
      </p>
      <div class="not-prose flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-2">
        <a
          href="https://www.instagram.com/teaandtoastblog/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 bg-amber-800 text-white rounded-xl text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-amber-900 transition shadow-sm"
        >
          <span>Instagram @teaandtoastblog</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 bg-white border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 rounded-xl text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-stone-50 transition shadow-sm"
        >
          <span>Contact Our Team</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
